<title>FINLAND: Metra to pay diesel deal from own funds.</title>
<headline>Metra to pay diesel deal from own funds.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish engineering group Metra Oy Ab said on Wednesday it would fund from its own reserves a 445 million markka cash payment to Italy's Fincantieri as part of a merger of diesel engine activities.</p>
<p>&quot;(We will pay) from our own funds,&quot; senior vice president and general counsel Timo Lehto said by telephone.</p>
<p>Asked how long he thought it would take for national competition authorities to approve the deal, he said he expected this to last two to three months: &quot;By end-March the thing should be cleared out,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +35 89 6805 0247</p>
